(Optimizing Photothermal Therapy for Acne: A Randomised Protocol Comparing Laser-Enhanced) Tj
T*
(versus Ultrasound-Assisted Nanoparticle Delivery) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Acne vulgaris treatment using photothermal approaches targets sebaceous structures with) Tj
T*
(minimal systemic exposure. This randomised study will compare two delivery mechanisms for) Tj
T*
(enhanced gold nanoparticles incorporated in lipid-based carriers to the skin of patients) Tj
T*
(with moderate-to-severe acne. One group will receive fractional CO2 laser microperforation) Tj
T*
(of the epidermis prior to nanoparticle application, while the second group will undergo) Tj
T*
(ultrasound-assisted transdermal delivery. Following nanoparticle deposition, all) Tj
T*
(participants will receive thermal laser treatment to activate photothermal destruction of) Tj
T*
(targeted follicular structures. Clinical assessments will document lesion counts across) Tj
T*
(comedonal, inflammatory, and cystic categories, as well as photographic documentation of) Tj
T*
(scarring. Skin biopsies will characterise histological changes including follicular damage) Tj
T*
(and collagen remodelling. Blood and urine analyses will quantify systemic absorption of) Tj
T*
(gold nanoparticles. Safety monitoring will track adverse reactions, tolerability scores,) Tj
T*
(and post-treatment recovery. This study aims to clarify whether mechanical barrier) Tj
T*
(disruption via fractional ablation enhances therapeutic delivery and efficacy compared to) Tj
T*
(acoustic delivery methods.) Tj
